## Azure DevOps & Cloud Learning Guide (2 Months)

This guide is designed to help you become a DevOps specialist with a focus on Azure and Linux in just 2 months. It includes a structured learning path, course requirements, recommendations, and helpful skills to acquire along the way.

---

### **Course Requirements**
- **Laptop/PC** (4GB+ RAM, internet access)
- **Azure Free Account** ([Sign up here](https://azure.microsoft.com/free/))
- **GitHub Account** ([Sign up here](https://github.com/))
- **Basic Programming Knowledge** (Python, Bash, or PowerShell recommended)
- **Willingness to Learn & Practice**

---

### **Learning Roadmap (8 Weeks)**

#### **Weeks 1-2: Linux Fundamentals**
- Linux installation (VM, WSL, or cloud VM)
- Basic commands, file system, permissions
- Shell scripting basics
- Recommended: [Linux Journey](https://linuxjourney.com/), [The Linux Command Line](https://linuxcommand.org/)

#### **Weeks 3-4: Azure Cloud Basics**
- Azure portal overview
- Core Azure services (VMs, Storage, Networking)
- Resource groups, ARM templates
- Recommended: [Microsoft Learn: Azure Fundamentals](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/azure-fundamentals/)

#### **Weeks 5-6: DevOps Concepts & Tools**
- What is DevOps? CI/CD basics
- Source control with Git & GitHub
- Azure DevOps: Boards, Repos, Pipelines
- Recommended: [Azure DevOps Labs](https://azuredevopslabs.com/), [Microsoft Learn: DevOps](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/devops-fundamentals/)

#### **Weeks 7-8: Automation & Advanced Topics**
- Infrastructure as Code (IaC): ARM, Bicep, Terraform
- Containerization: Docker basics
- Monitoring & Security basics
- Practice: Build a CI/CD pipeline for a sample app
- Recommended: [Terraform on Azure](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/developer/terraform/), [Docker Getting Started](https://docs.docker.com/get-started/)

---

### **Helpful Skills to Develop**
- Problem-solving & troubleshooting
- Scripting (Bash, PowerShell, Python)
- Understanding of networking basics
- Familiarity with version control (Git)
- Basic knowledge of containers (Docker)
- Cloud cost management

---


### **Azure Certification Courses Required**

- **AZ-900: Microsoft Azure Fundamentals**
  - [Microsoft Learn Path](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/azure-fundamentals/)
  - Covers: Cloud concepts, Azure services, security, privacy, compliance, and pricing

- **AZ-104: Microsoft Azure Administrator**
  - [Microsoft Learn Path](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/azure-administrator/)
  - Covers: Managing Azure subscriptions, resources, storage, virtual machines, networking, and identities

- **AZ-400: Designing and Implementing Microsoft DevOps Solutions**
  - [Microsoft Learn Path](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/training/paths/azure-devops/)
  - Covers: DevOps practices, CI/CD, source control, security, compliance, infrastructure as code, and monitoring

---

### **Additional Recommendations**
- Join online communities (Reddit, Stack Overflow, Azure forums)
- Follow Azure & DevOps blogs and YouTube channels
- Work on small projects and document your progress
- Consider certification: [AZ-900](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/certifications/exams/az-900/), [AZ-104](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/certifications/exams/az-104/), [AZ-400](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/certifications/exams/az-400/)

---

**Stay consistent, practice daily, and you'll be well on your way to becoming an Azure DevOps specialist!**
